      "body": "## Summary\n\nAn approved operator transfers a veNFT to `address(0)` because `_transferFrom` omits the zero-address guard. Ownership is set to the zero address without executing `_burn`, approvals are cleared, and `withdraw` becomes unreachable. The escrowed ERC‑20 tokens remain trapped forever.\n\n## Finding Description\n\n`VotingEscrow._transferFrom` asserts in NatSpec that it \"Throws if `_to` is the zero address,\" yet the implementation lacks that require. Any owner-approved operator (via `approve` or `setApprovalForAll`) can invoke `transferFrom/safeTransferFrom` with `_to = address(0)` when the NFT is not attached or actively voted. The flow clears approvals, moves delegates, and sets `idToOwner[_tokenId] = address(0)`; it never calls `_burn`, so the underlying lock persists. Since future `withdraw` requires owner/approval, and no one owns the token, funds are irretrievable.\n\nCode references (existing repository code):\n\n```338:368:/Users/almanax-1/repos/Code4rena/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol\n/// @dev Exeute transfer of a NFT.\n///      Throws unless `msg.sender` is the current owner, an authorized operator, or the approved\n///      address for this NFT. (NOTE: `msg.sender` not allowed in internal function so pass `_sender`.)\n///      Throws if `_to` is the zero address.\n///      Throws if `_from` is not the current owner.\n///      Throws if `_tokenId` is not a valid NFT.\nfunction _transferFrom(\n    address _from,\n    address _to,\n    uint _tokenId,\n    address _sender\n) internal notPartnerNFT(_tokenId) {\n    require(attachments[_tokenId] == 0 && !voted[_tokenId], \"ATT\");\n    require(_isApprovedOrOwner(_sender, _tokenId), \"NAO\");\n    _clearApproval(_from, _tokenId);\n    _removeTokenFrom(_from, _tokenId);\n    VotingDelegationLib.moveTokenDelegates(cpData, delegates(_from), delegates(_to), _tokenId, ownerOf);\n    _addTokenTo(_to, _tokenId);\n    ownership_change[_tokenId] = block.number;\n    emit Transfer(_from, _to, _tokenId);\n}\n```\n\n```429:436:/Users/almanax-1/repos/Code4rena/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol\nfunction safeTransferFrom(\n    address _from,\n    address _to,\n    uint _tokenId,\n    bytes memory _data\n) public {\n    _transferFrom(_from, _to, _tokenId, msg.sender);\n    // onERC721Received check follows for contracts\n}\n```\n\n```550:560:/Users/almanax-1/repos/Code4rena/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol\nfunction _removeTokenFrom(address _from, uint _tokenId) internal {\n    assert(idToOwner[_tokenId] == _from);\n    idToOwner[_tokenId] = address(0);\n    _removeTokenFromOwnerList(_from, _tokenId);\n    ownerToNFTokenCount[_from] -= 1;\n}\n```\n\n```322:332:/Users/almanax-1/repos/Code4rena/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol\nfunction _isApprovedOrOwner(address _spender, uint _tokenId) internal view returns (bool) {\n    address owner = idToOwner[_tokenId];\n    bool spenderIsOwner = owner == _spender;\n    bool spenderIsApproved = _spender == idToApprovals[_tokenId];\n    bool spenderIsApprovedForAll = (ownerToOperators[owner])[_spender];\n    return spenderIsOwner || spenderIsApproved || spenderIsApprovedForAll;\n}\n```\n\n```915:942:/Users/almanax-1/repos/Code4rena/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol\nfunction withdraw(uint _tokenId) external nonreentrant {\n    assert(_isApprovedOrOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId));\n    require(attachments[_tokenId] == 0 && !voted[_tokenId], \"ATT\");\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory _locked = locked[_tokenId];\n    require(!_locked.isPermanent, \"!NORM\");\n    require(block.timestamp >= _locked.end, \"!EXP\");\n    uint value = uint(int256(_locked.amount));\n    locked[_tokenId] = IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false);\n    _checkpoint(_tokenId, _locked, IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false));\n    assert(IERC20(token).transfer(msg.sender, value));\n    _burn(_tokenId);\n}\n```\n\n```509:517:/Users/almanax-1/repos/Code4rena/2025-10-hybra-finance/ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol\nfunction _mint(address _to, uint _tokenId) internal returns (bool) {\n    assert(_to != address(0));\n    VotingDelegationLib.moveTokenDelegates(cpData, address(0), delegates(_to), _tokenId, ownerOf);\n    _addTokenTo(_to, _tokenId);\n    emit Transfer(address(0), _to, _tokenId);\n    return true;\n}\n```\n\nBehavior alignment: The implementation contradicts its own documentation and standard ERC‑721 practice about forbidding zero-address transfers. No recovery or admin path exists to withdraw after ownership becomes zero.\n\n## Impact and Likelihood Explanation\n\nImpact: An approved operator transfers a veNFT to the zero address and permanently prevents any withdrawal, trapping all escrowed tokens in the contract with no owner capable of satisfying `withdraw` preconditions.\n\nLikelihood: Users frequently grant operator approvals; the transfer only requires the NFT to be unattached and not actively voted. This path executes in one transaction and requires no unusual on-chain conditions.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nEnforce zero-address rejection in all NFT transfer flows and route destruction through `_burn` only.\n\n- Add a guard at the start of `_transferFrom` and both `safeTransferFrom` overloads:\n  - `require(_to != address(0), \"ZA\");`\n- Optionally add an explicit `burn(uint tokenId)` that is owner/approved-only and performs proper state cleanup.\n- Add non-zero guards for external recipient addresses in integration points (e.g., treasury `Team` addresses) to prevent accidental sends to zero.\n\nExample minimal edits:\n\n```solidity\n// inside _transferFrom(...)\nrequire(_to != address(0), \"ZA\");\n```\n\n```solidity\n// inside safeTransferFrom(...)\nrequire(_to != address(0), \"ZA\");\n```",
